.SH NAME
ivcap-genome-import - Import an NCBI genome package into IVCAP


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBivcap genome import ACCESSION [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Import an NCBI genome data package as an IVCAP artifact.

.PP
The package is downloaded to a temporary file which is removed after upload; no local package is
left behind. The same --include, --chromosomes, --assembly-version and --fast-zip-validation options
as 'genome download' control the package. The imported artifact receives an assembly report
aspect and an RO-Crate 1.2 archive manifest aspect.

.PP
The manifest records a license for the data. NCBI states none: it places no restrictions itself,
but submitters may claim rights that it cannot assess. By default the manifest therefore links to
NCBI's data usage policy, which is a pointer and not a license grant. Use --license to state another.

.PP
The imported data is public NCBI data, so the artifact and both aspects get the open policies
(ivcap.open.artifact and ivcap.open.metadata). Use --policy to give all three another policy.

.PP
If an aspect request fails after upload, the error names the uploaded artifact so it can be repaired.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--assembly-version\fP=""
	Version policy [a versioned ACCESSION is used as given, an unversioned one means its current version]: 'current' (same as 'latest') ignores the version in ACCESSION and takes the current one; 'all' selects every version and is rejected here unless there is exactly one

.PP
\fB--chromosomes\fP=[]
	Limit the genome FASTA to these chromosomes (comma-separated names, or 'all'); the names are passed to NCBI unchanged

.PP
\fB--chunk-size\fP=10000000
	Chunk size in bytes for splitting large files: at least 65536, or -1 to upload without chunking

.PP
\fB--fast-zip-validation\fP[=false]
	Only check the zip's directory after the download, not every file in it

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for import

.PP
\fB--include\fP=[genome]
	Files to include, comma-separated: genome (genomic FASTA), rna (transcripts), protein (amino acid sequences), cds (nucleotide coding sequences), gff3 or gtf (annotation), gbff (GenBank flat file), seq-report (per-sequence report), all (every type, use alone) or none (metadata only, use alone)

.PP
\fB--license\fP=""
	License of the imported data, recorded in the manifest: an SPDX identifier such as CC0-1.0, a license URL, or 'undefined' [a link to NCBI's data usage policy, which states no license]

.PP
\fB--manifest-schema\fP="urn:ivcap:schema:artifact.archive-manifest.1"
	Schema URN for the RO-Crate manifest aspect

.PP
\fB-n\fP, \fB--name\fP=""
	Artifact name [zip file name]

.PP
\fB--ncbi-api-key\fP=""
	NCBI API key, which raises NCBI's rate limit [NCBI_API_KEY]

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--policy\fP=""
	Policy for the artifact and both aspects [urn:ivcap:policy:ivcap.open.artifact and urn:ivcap:policy:ivcap.open.metadata, as the data is public]

.PP
\fB--report-schema\fP="urn:ivcap:schema:ncbi.assembly-data-report.1"
	Schema URN for the assembly report aspect


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--access-token\fP=""
	Access token to use for authentication with API server [IVCAP_ACCESS_TOKEN]

.PP
\fB--context\fP=""
	Context (deployment) to use

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Set logging level to DEBUG

.PP
\fB--no-history\fP[=false]
	Do not store history

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	Set format for displaying output [json, yaml]

.PP
\fB--silent\fP[=false]
	Do not show any progress information

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30
	Max. number of seconds to wait for completion


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  ivcap genome import GCF_000001735.4
  ivcap genome import GCF_000001735.4 --include genome,gff3,seq-report
  ivcap --output json genome import GCF_000001735.4 --policy urn:ivcap:policy:...
.EE


